 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
 stroke-linejoin="round">
 &lt;rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2">&lt;/rect>
 &lt;path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1">&lt;/path>
 &lt;/svg>
 &lt;span class="copy-feedback">&lt;/span>
 &lt;/button>
 &lt;div class="codeblock-content">&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nt">switch&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>- &lt;span class="nt">platform&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">gpio&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">pin&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">GPIOXX&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">name&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;Living Room Dehumidifier&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w">&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">binary_sensor&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>- &lt;span class="nt">platform&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">gpio&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">pin&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">GPIOXX&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">name&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;Living Room Dehumidifier Toggle Button&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>

&lt;p>With this file you can already perform some basic tasks. You can control the ON/OFF state of the dehumidifier in your
living room from Home Assistant&amp;rsquo;s front-end. But in many cases, controlling everything strictly from the frontend is
not desirable. That&amp;rsquo;s why you&amp;rsquo;ve also installed a simple push button next to the dehumidifier wired to pin GPIOXX.
A simple push of this button should toggle the state of the dehumidifier.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Templates</title><link>https://bharvey88.github.io/esphome-docs/automations/templates/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bharvey88.github.io/esphome-docs/automations/templates/</guid><description>&lt;a class="anchor" id="config-lambda" role="none">&lt;/a>

&lt;p>&lt;em>Templates&lt;/em> (also known as &lt;em>lambdas&lt;/em>) allow you to do almost &lt;em>anything&lt;/em> in ESPHome. For example, if you want to only
perform a certain automation if a certain complex formula evaluates to true, you can do that with templates. Let&amp;rsquo;s look
at an example first:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="code-block">
 &lt;button class="copy-button" aria-label="Copy code">
 &lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
 role="none"
 width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
 stroke-linejoin="round">
 &lt;rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2">&lt;/rect>
 &lt;path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1">&lt;/path>
 &lt;/svg>
 &lt;span class="copy-feedback">&lt;/span>
 &lt;/button>
 &lt;div class="codeblock-content">&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nt">binary_sensor&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>- &lt;span class="nt">platform&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">gpio&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">name&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;Cover End Stop&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">id&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">top_end_stop&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w">&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">cover&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>- &lt;span class="nt">platform&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">template&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">name&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">Living Room Cover&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="nt">lambda&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">:&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>!&lt;span class="l">lambda |-&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">if (id(top_end_stop).state) {&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">return COVER_OPEN;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>}&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">else {&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>&lt;span class="l">return COVER_CLOSED;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="w">
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="w"> &lt;/span>}&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>

&lt;p>What&amp;rsquo;s happening here? First, we define a binary sensor (notably with &lt;code>id: top_end_stop&lt;/code> ) and then a
&lt;a href="https://bharvey88.github.io/esphome-docs/components/cover/template/">template cover&lt;/a>. (If you&amp;rsquo;re new to Home Assistant, a &amp;lsquo;cover&amp;rsquo; is something
like a window blind, a roller shutter, or a garage door.) The &lt;em>state&lt;/em> of the template cover is controlled by a template,
or &amp;ldquo;lambda&amp;rdquo;. In lambdas, you&amp;rsquo;re just writing C++ code and therefore the name lambda is used instead of Home Assistant&amp;rsquo;s
&amp;ldquo;template&amp;rdquo; lingo to avoid confusion. Regardless, don&amp;rsquo;t let lambdas scare you just because you saw &amp;ldquo;C++&amp;rdquo; &amp;ndash; writing
lambdas is not that hard! Here&amp;rsquo;s a bit of a primer:&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>